1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,211
Stuck on a beach

2
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:02,475
with only one tree,

3
00:00:02,515 --> 00:00:04,039
you'd sit under it.

4
00:00:04,079 --> 00:00:04,751
Don't.

5
00:00:04,791 --> 00:00:06,315
It's a manchineel.

6
00:00:06,355 --> 00:00:07,792
It has small green apples,

7
00:00:07,832 --> 00:00:08,643
and a red band

8
00:00:08,683 --> 00:00:10,632
someone painted on the trunk.

9
00:00:10,672 --> 00:00:12,409
Here's what that band is for.

10
00:00:12,449 --> 00:00:13,247
A storm hits,

11
00:00:13,287 --> 00:00:15,449
so you shelter under the leaves.

12
00:00:15,489 --> 00:00:17,139
Each one holds a milky sap,

13
00:00:17,179 --> 00:00:18,203
and the rain drips it

14
00:00:18,243 --> 00:00:19,554
onto your skin.

15
00:00:19,594 --> 00:00:21,756
Soon you're covered in blisters.

16
00:00:21,796 --> 00:00:23,232
The next day you're starving,

17
00:00:23,272 --> 00:00:25,009
and the apples smell good.

18
00:00:25,049 --> 00:00:26,060
One bite is sweet,

19
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:27,411
for a second.

20
00:00:27,451 --> 00:00:28,262
Then your throat burns

21
00:00:28,302 --> 00:00:29,400
and tightens.

22
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,877
In Spanish, that fruit is

23
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:32,654
the little apple of death.

24
00:00:32,694 --> 00:00:34,117
Later, nature calls,

25
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:35,394
and you grab a handful

26
00:00:35,434 --> 00:00:36,532
of soft leaves.

27
00:00:36,572 --> 00:00:37,996
Same sap, same blisters,

28
00:00:38,036 --> 00:00:39,134
much worse place.

29
00:00:39,174 --> 00:00:40,186
That night you're cold,

30
00:00:40,226 --> 00:00:41,749
so you light its wood.

31
00:00:41,789 --> 00:00:42,813
The smoke stings your eyes

32
00:00:42,853 --> 00:00:44,803
until you can barely see.

33
00:00:44,843 --> 00:00:45,428
Next time,

34
00:00:45,468 --> 00:00:46,992
just sit in the sand.

35
00:00:47,032 --> 00:00:47,843
Subscribe for more

36
00:00:47,883 --> 00:00:49,547
of nature's warnings.
